.\nThis is an internal quality-control score — NOT Facebook's algorithm score.\nScore how a real human scrolling their phone feed would react to this card.\n\n─── POST DETAILS ───────────────────────────────────────────\nHEADLINE:  {headline}\nCATEGORY:  {category}\nSOURCE:    {source}\nSUMMARY:   {summary}\nIMAGE:     {\"Card image exists\" if has_image else \"No image (text-only post)\"}\n{mobile_note}\n─── SCORING CRITERIA ───────────────────────────────────────\nScore each criterion honestly. Do not inflate scores.\n\n1. Headline clarity       (0–20): Is the headline sharp, specific, and scannable?\n   A score of 20 means anyone reads it and instantly knows exactly what happened.\n   Deduct for vague language, jargon, missing subject, or ambiguity.\n\n2. Visual impact          (0–20): Would this card stop a thumb while scrolling?\n   A score of 20 means the card is visually striking with a compelling photo.\n   Deduct for no image, blurry photo, poor contrast, or boring composition.\n   {\"Deduct heavily — no image.\" if not has_image else \"\"}\n\n3. Story importance       (0–20): Does this story matter to a general audience?\n   A score of 20 means millions of people would want to know this right now.\n   Deduct for niche topics, minor local stories, or low-stakes content.\n\n4. Mobile readability     (0–15): Readable on a phone within 1–2 seconds?\n   A score of 15 means the headline is large, clear, and immediately legible.\n   Deduct for too many words, small text, or cluttered layout.\n\n5. Emotional interest     (0–10): Does this post create curiosity, urgency, or empathy?\n   A score of 10 means a reader feels compelled to tap or share.\n   Deduct for dry, flat, or overly technical framing.\n\n6. Brand consistency      (0–10): Does this look like Global Pulse News?\n   A score of 10 means navy+white+red palette, professional badge, clean footer.\n   Deduct for anything that looks generic, off-brand, or amateurish.\n\n7. Professional quality   (0–5): Is the overall card clean and error-free?\n   A score of 5 means no visible clutter, overflow, or layout issues.\n   Deduct for any obvious visual errors or text overflow.\n\n─── OUTPUT FORMAT ───────────────────────────────────────────\nRespond ONLY with valid JSON. No markdown, no explanation outside the JSON.\n\n{{\n  \"headline_clarity\":    <int 0-20>,\n  \"visual_impact\":       <int 0-20>,\n  \"story_importance\":    <int 0-20>,\n  \"mobile_readability\":  <int 0-15>,\n  \"emotional_interest\":  <int 0-10>,\n  \"brand_consistency\":   <int 0-10>,\n  \"professional_quality\": <int 0-5>,\n  \"notes\": \"<one sentence per criterion, separated by | >\"\n}}\n\"\"\"\n\n\n# ── Ollama call ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef _call_ollama(prompt: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Call Ollama chat completions and return the raw text response.\"\"\"\n    base_url = (config.OLLAMA_BASE_URL or \"http://localhost:11434/v1\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    model    = config.OLLAMA_MODEL or \"llama3.2\"\n\n    payload = {\n        \"model\":    model,\n        \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n        \"stream\":   False,\n        \"options\":  {\n            \"temperature\": 0.2,   # low temperature = consistent, non-creative scoring\n            \"top_p\": 0.9,\n        },\n    }\n\n    r = requests.post(\n        f\"{base_url}/chat/completions\",\n        json=payload,\n        timeout=45,\n    )\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    data = r.json()\n    return data[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"].strip()\n\n\n# ── Response parser ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef _parse_response(raw: str, story: Story) -> AttentionResult:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse the LLM JSON response into an AttentionResult.\n    Handles common LLM formatting quirks (markdown fences, trailing commas).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Strip markdown code fences if present\n    text = re.sub(r\"```(?:json)?\", \"\", raw).strip()\n    # Remove trailing